<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and all three repurchase agreements, through which it had sought to drain 1.682 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    346 days   20.97 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   20.97 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   20.95 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    800 million     31 days   19.80 pct</p>
<p>    300 million     21 days   19.67 pct</p>
<p>    132 million	1 day    18.95 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
